Real-World Examples
SQL Queries are based on relational algebra operations:

SELECT corresponds to Projection.
WHERE clause corresponds to Selection.
JOIN corresponds to Join.
UNION, INTERSECT, EXCEPT correspond to set operations.
Query optimization engines use relational algebra trees to optimize execution plans.

Common Misunderstandings and Mistakes
Relational algebra operates on sets, so duplicates are eliminated unless explicitly handled.
Attributes in relations must be compatible for set operations like union and difference.
Cartesian product can produce very large relations if not filtered properly.
Join conditions are crucial to avoid unintended large datasets.
